
	UNRESOLVED BUGS

	(As of version 2025-12-23)

	Thanks to all submitters!

	BUG: Compiler enters infinite loop on certain valid C89 code
	     The compiler hangs indefinitely (requires kill) when compiling
	     certain valid C89 constructs. Affected test cases:
	     - t_array_complex.c (complex array operations)
	     - t_const_expr.c (constant expressions)
	     - t_global.c (global variable initialization)
	     - t_state_machine.c (enum with function pointer arrays)
	     Workaround: None. These patterns should be avoided until fixed.

